WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.410
Welcome to our used sold as new product compliance training.

00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:08.526
A used sold as new product condition issue occurs when a customer receives a product

00:00:08.526 --> 00:00:11.254
that isn't in the new condition they expected.

00:00:11.254 --> 00:00:16.711
If a product's detail page states the product is new when the customer receives the product,

00:00:16.711 --> 00:00:18.757
it must be in new condition.

00:00:18.757 --> 00:00:22.850
Noncompliance with Amazon's preventing product condition issues and condition guidelines policies

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:26.260
may affect your ability to sell in the Amazon store.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:32.029
Customers may perceive a product to have been previously used when it's scratched,

00:00:32.029 --> 00:00:37.519
scuffed, dirty, odorous, stained, or has other imperfections that indicate it's been used.

00:00:37.519 --> 00:00:40.897
Its packaging has been previously opened or damaged.

00:00:40.897 --> 00:00:47.231
The product isn't in its original unopened packaging or when the product or packaging seal

00:00:47.231 --> 00:00:48.920
is missing or broken.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:54.123
Let's meet Sophia, who sells multiple products in the Amazon store.

00:00:54.123 --> 00:01:00.209
She monitors what her customers say about her products by signing in to Seller Central

00:01:00.209 --> 00:01:04.266
and reviewing buyer messages using the buyer seller messaging service,

00:01:04.266 --> 00:01:07.917
customer feedback, product reviews, A to Z claims, returns,

00:01:07.917 --> 00:01:12.380
the customer complaint summary, and the voice of the customer dashboard.

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:16.498
Sophia ensures that she sets accurate expectations for her customers

00:01:16.498 --> 00:01:21.540
by clearly describing the condition of her products on the product detail pages.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.700
When she lists each of her products, Sophia makes sure that she chooses the correct

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:28.580
condition from the drop-down list.

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:32.740
She only chooses new if her product is truly in new condition.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.920
Note that not all stores have the option to list used products.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:43.209
Here are some tips to prevent noncompliance with Amazon's preventing product condition issues

00:01:43.209 --> 00:01:44.840
policy and condition guidelines.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:46.123
Tip 1.

00:01:46.123 --> 00:01:49.860
Describe your products and their packaging clearly on the product detail pages.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:51.225
Tip 2.

00:01:51.225 --> 00:01:55.980
Regularly carry out quality audits to review your quality control processes.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:57.256
Tip 3.

00:01:57.256 --> 00:02:01.789
Inspect your products to ensure they function correctly and match their descriptions

00:02:01.789 --> 00:02:03.300
on the detail pages.

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:04.592
Tip 4.

00:02:04.592 --> 00:02:09.440
Ensure your staff are trained to prevent issues with both new and returned products.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:10.643
Tip 5.

00:02:10.643 --> 00:02:14.620
Check to determine if your products have any defects or issues.

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:16.068
Tip 6.

00:02:16.068 --> 00:02:19.620
Select appropriate packaging and shipping for your product.

00:02:20.276 --> 00:02:21.917
Use bubble wrap and other

00:02:21.917 --> 00:02:26.840
protective packaging and ensure the packaging's design is suitable for the product and its handling.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:32.400
Customers often perceive products with damaged or open packaging to have been previously used.

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:33.769
Tip 7.

00:02:33.769 --> 00:02:38.640
Store your products where they'll remain clean, dry, and at the correct temperature.

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:39.742
Tip 8.

00:02:39.742 --> 00:02:44.800
Never return a product to sellable inventory when the product's seal has been broken

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:51.120
and always label and store your returned products separately from new products to avoid any confusion.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:56.467
Don't forget that you may only resell returned products as new if they meet the

00:02:56.467 --> 00:03:00.360
condition guidelines for a new product and show no signs of use.

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:05.686
You can find the condition guidelines by going to Seller Central and searching for condition

00:03:05.686 --> 00:03:09.020
guidelines in the search field at the top of the page.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:12.211
Remember to keep your account health from

00:03:12.211 --> 00:03:16.220
being negatively impacted by used sold as new product condition complaints.

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:17.707
Always ensure that

00:03:17.707 --> 00:03:22.740
your customer receives the product in the condition as described on the product detail page.

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:27.240
This concludes our training on used sold as new product compliance.

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:30.840
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon store!
